# Documentation

Last30days-news is a desktop-style reader for the last 30 days of technology news. It collects RSS feeds and other sources into one database, merges duplicate stories, and can add cited AI summaries.

The same code runs in three places:

| Target | Database | First password | Reset |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Local | SQLite file | `last30` | `/reset` from this machine |
| Vercel | Turso libSQL | `L30_INITIAL_PASSWORD` | Disabled |
| VPS or Docker | SQLite file | `L30_INITIAL_PASSWORD` | Disabled |

<Diagram
	name="run-modes"
	alt="Local, VPS and Vercel run modes, showing the browser, app process and database for each"
	caption="The database and password policy change with the target. The reader stays the same."
/>

## Install

Pick the command for your system. Each one installs the latest release and starts with the default settings. You can change the port, data directory and password later.

### Windows

<CopyCommand command={`irm ${INSTALL_PS1_URL} | iex`} label="PowerShell" />

### macOS and Linux

<CopyCommand command={`curl -fsSL ${INSTALL_SH_URL} | sh`} label="Terminal" />

### Run without installing

<CopyCommand command="npx last30days-news" label="Node.js" />

The first local run starts at `http://127.0.0.1:4477` and uses the password `last30`. Change it in Settings after you sign in.

